From 450943566362773d0ed6c67d0bd783ccef7a92b4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dev <dev@local>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:58:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/24] feat(debug): read frame timings on the screen, because
 adb cannot reach this device

The phone this ships to runs HarmonyOS, whose USB debug function is HDC on the
vendor interface (ff/50) rather than the Android debug interface adb looks for
(ff/42), and whose wireless debugging offers no pairing entry. `dumpsys gfxinfo`
is therefore unavailable on the device that matters, so the numbers have to come
from the only clock left and be read off the screen.

- frameSamples: samples native rAF deltas into a preallocated ring buffer - one
  float per frame, no allocation, no React - and reports p50/p90/p99, worst, jank
  share, long tasks and heap. It samples through the limiter's saved native rAF,
  otherwise it would measure our own cap instead of the device. Gaps over 250ms
  are excluded: those are the app being backgrounded, not dropped frames.
- FrameStatsHud: polls the sampler twice a second and draws the result. Toggled
  by holding the top-left corner, because a landscape phone has no keyboard to
  reach Alt+Shift+D with. The listener sits in the window capture phase and never
  prevents the event, so it cannot steal input from the player.
